<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21331] ptlrpc: forward clock step makes targets evict all exports</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21331</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When the clock on a server steps forward, every target on that server&lt;br/&gt;
evicts every export it has not heard from since the step. The clock can&lt;br/&gt;
step when a VM resumes from suspend, when chrony corrects a bad RTC, or&lt;br/&gt;
after "date -s". The console shows:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;lustre-MDT0000: haven't heard from client ... in 318 seconds. I think it's dead, and I am evicting it.
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both clients and the MDT OSP exports on an OST are evicted, within about&lt;br/&gt;
one second of each other.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Cause"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Cause&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The ping evictor keeps export times on the wall clock.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;exp_deadline&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;exp_last_request_time&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;obd_eviction_timer&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
are set from &lt;tt&gt;ktime_get_real_seconds()&lt;/tt&gt; in &lt;tt&gt;__class_new_export()&lt;/tt&gt;,&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;rev_import_init()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;ptlrpc_update_export_timer()&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;ping_evictor_main()&lt;/tt&gt; compares them with the same clock. A step of S&lt;br/&gt;
seconds makes every export look S seconds idle at the same time. When S&lt;br/&gt;
is larger than the deadline margin (about 100s with default timeouts),&lt;br/&gt;
all of these exports are evicted together.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Fix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;tt&gt;ktime_get_seconds()&lt;/tt&gt; for these values. They are only compared&lt;br/&gt;
with each other or printed as a difference, so they do not need wall&lt;br/&gt;
clock time. &lt;tt&gt;rq_deadline&lt;/tt&gt;/&lt;tt&gt;rq_arrival_time&lt;/tt&gt; (adaptive timeouts,&lt;br/&gt;
early replies) and &lt;tt&gt;scp_last_request&lt;/tt&gt; also use wall clock time, but&lt;br/&gt;
they do not cause evictions and are not changed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Reproducer"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproducer&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mount a filesystem with an OSS on its own node and write from a client&lt;br/&gt;
to OST0000. On the OSS, stop chronyd/ntpd and step the clock forward&lt;br/&gt;
300 seconds:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;date -s "+300 seconds"
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Within a few seconds the MDT OSP exports and the client are evicted from&lt;br/&gt;
the OST. The new test replay-single test_225 does this and checks that&lt;br/&gt;
no target logs "haven't heard from client" and no client is evicted.&lt;br/&gt;
It fails on unpatched master.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
